{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1540707-family-inheritences-we-know-about","id":1540707,"title":"Family Inheritences We Know About","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-19T08:41:18-07:00","id":1540707,"title":"Family Inheritences We Know About","content":"Inheritances we know about from the Blog posts:<ul><li><b>Get of Lyka</b> - Their punch and claw attacks are truly devastating, gaining the Brutal and Wounding tags.</li> <li><b>Hydes</b> - They can bottle their spells by embracing their curse, activating the powers from their stored magic in the future, for free, reflexively. What\u2019s more, their wild forms are so gargantuan and cumbersome, every attack they make comes with the Wrecking tag, enabling them to demolish people, objects, and even buildings with ease.</li> <li><b>Vodnik </b>- When they seek to acquire an item, they can bleed away their curse and transform their magical blight into wealth. And this need not be money; wealth is whatever the other party in a deal or trade desires, from information to dreams, to more esoteric fare. What\u2019s more, Vodn\u00edci in their wild forms are quite capable of breathing underwater, lurking unseen until it\u2019s time to slide onto shore.</li> <li><b>Nephilim</b> - Once in a while they can quickly and quietly duck into and out of a nearby Battleground, appearing in a location in the real world they personally know about moments later.</li> <li><b>Battleground Angels</b> - They are good at leading and organizing teams. As a result, teamwork actions are more effective, causing the overall difficulty of the task to drop.</li> <li><b>Munificent</b> - Whenever they try to persuade someone, they\u2019re not only a little better at it than most people, but they have a unique Trick which allows them to find out what their target\u2019s innermost desire is, and what they would do to get it. They become inadvertent confidants of just about anyone, which gives them the perfect opportunity to give that person their fondest wish, or blackmail them as leverage to get what the Outcast truly wants.</li> </ul><br /> Inheritences from the Ashcan (Summarized by me):<ul><li><b>Primal</b> - Add Entanglement in Hits to hunt/tracking actions before the roll. Gain an additional Evidence once per session.</li> <li><b>Outcast </b>- Add Entanglement in Hits to Persuade actions against a stranger before the roll.</li> <li><b>Maven</b> - Once per Scene while incorporeal, apply Overstimulating as a Major Complication.</li> <li><b>House B\u00e1thory </b>- Once per scene, cover face in blood to resolve 1 status effect.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T10:21:33-07:00","id":1540711,"title":"","content":"thanks for thAT","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}